    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107162" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεξ-αναδύομαι</span></b> , 
			Med.
		, with aor. 2
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έδυν,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dive out and emerge, come from
				under secretly</i> or <i>gradually,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάθρῃ ὑπεξαναδὺς πολιῆς ἁλός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.352
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. κεφαλῇ</span>
			<i>duck</i> or <i>stoop</i> so as to avoid a blow, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				22.123
			</span></i>.</div>
